  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 156 AM MDT Sat Aug 15 2026\n\nRidging will continue to develop over the desert southwest early \nnext week. The warmer temperatures and subsidence will decrease the \noverall coverage of precipitation, but there will still be enough \nmoisture left underneath the ridge to produce daily rounds of \nshowers and storms. \n\nModel agreement is starting to increase mid-week, with the LREF \nshowing a slight westward shift in the centroid of the ridge. \nHowever, this shift should be too subtle and brief to mark a pattern \ntransition as model consensus brings the ridge overhead again late \nweek. While a slight downtick in storm coverage can be expected, NBM \nguidance is running a touch dry and will most likely trend up a tad \nin the coming days if the current pattern shown by ensemble means \nmanages to hold. Regardless of the exact location of the ridge, \nabove normal heights will translate to hot temperatures each \nafternoon, generally running 5 to 10 degrees above average mid to \nlate week.",
